From 4f7632d7f283bb38396a44d775b6a80afcd62f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:53:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] public-rpc consumer interface: bounded
 eth_getProof/eth_getBlockByHash proof material, pending nonce and tip quote,
 labelled by class

eth_getProof (address, at most maxProofKeys distinct storage words, EIP-1898 or bare-hash block, no pending) and
eth_getBlockByHash (headers only) serve B's witness gateway, which verifies them against its own signed roots; the role
labels them X-Enclave-Rpc-Class: proof-material-unverified. eth_getTransactionCount accepts "pending" (mempool-unverified)
and eth_maxPriorityFeePerGas takes no parameters (fee-quote-unverified) for E's profile broadcast. Composed E2Es run the
packaged role under the runner with B's pinned gateway/Helios/witness-check and E's pinned site modules on reth v2.8.0.
---
